# Checking a beam's bending stress
#
# Four designs of a simply supported rectangular beam carry a point load at
# mid-span. Backward rules (<=) compute each beam's bending moment, section
# modulus, bending stress and safety factor, and compare the stress with the
# allowable stress. eyeron answers three queries: three designs are safe and
# the overloaded floor beam is not. It shows backward rules with N3 math
# built-ins, and log:query to choose what is printed.

@base <https://eyereasoner.github.io/eye/reasoning/beam-bending-safety/beam-bending-safety.n3> .

# For each beam design we have:
# - span L          (metres)
# - mid-span load P (kN)
# - width  b        (metres)
# - height h        (metres)
# - allowable stress sigma_allow (kN/m², given these units)
#
# Mechanics:
# - maximum bending moment: M_max = P * L / 4
# - section modulus of a rectangle: S = b * h^2 / 6
# - bending stress: sigma = M_max / S
# - safety factor: sigma_allow / sigma
#
# A design is safe if sigma ≤ sigma_allow and failing otherwise.

@prefix : <http://example.org/beam#> .
@prefix beam: <http://example.org/beam#> .
@prefix thm: <http://example.org/theorem#> .
@prefix rel: <http://example.org/rel#> .

@prefix math: <http://www.w3.org/2000/10/swap/math#> .
@prefix list: <http://www.w3.org/2000/10/swap/list#> .
@prefix log: <http://www.w3.org/2000/10/swap/log#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .

# The vocabulary: a class of beam designs, the given quantities (span L,
# pointLoad P, width b, height h, allowableStress sigma_allow) and the
# derived ones (maxMoment M_max, sectionModulus S, bendingStress sigma,
# safetyFactor, isSafe as a boolean).
:BeamDesign a rdfs:Class .

:span a rdf:Property .
:pointLoad a rdf:Property .
:width a rdf:Property .
:height a rdf:Property .
:allowableStress a rdf:Property .

:maxMoment a rdf:Property .
:sectionModulus a rdf:Property .
:bendingStress a rdf:Property .
:safetyFactor a rdf:Property .
:isSafe a rdf:Property .

# Backward rules for derived quantities: each is computed when asked for.

# Maximum bending moment for simply supported beam with mid-span load:
# M_max = P * L / 4
{
    ?B :maxMoment ?M .
} <= {
    ?B a :BeamDesign ;
        :span ?L ;
        :pointLoad ?P .

    (?P ?L) math:product ?PL .
    (?PL 4.0) math:quotient ?M .
} .

# Section modulus of rectangular section:
# S = b * h^2 / 6
{
    ?B :sectionModulus ?S .
} <= {
    ?B a :BeamDesign ;
        :width ?b ;
        :height ?h .

    (?h 2) math:exponentiation ?h2 .
    (?b ?h2) math:product ?bh2 .
    (?bh2 6.0) math:quotient ?S .
} .

# Bending stress:
# sigma = M_max / S
{
    ?B :bendingStress ?sigma .
} <= {
    ?B :maxMoment ?M ;
        :sectionModulus ?S .

    (?M ?S) math:quotient ?sigma .
} .

# Safety factor:
# safetyFactor = allowableStress / sigma
{
    ?B :safetyFactor ?sf .
} <= {
    ?B :bendingStress ?sigma ;
        :allowableStress ?allow .

    (?allow ?sigma) math:quotient ?sf .
} .

# Safety classification:
# safe iff sigma ≤ sigma_allow
{
    ?B :isSafe true .
} <= {
    ?B :bendingStress ?sigma ;
        :allowableStress ?allow .
    ?sigma math:notGreaterThan ?allow .
} .

{
    ?B :isSafe false .
} <= {
    ?B :bendingStress ?sigma ;
        :allowableStress ?allow .
    ?sigma math:greaterThan ?allow .
} .

# Example beam designs, all with the same allowable stress of 12000:
# - ShelfLight: a short, lightly loaded shelf.
# - FloorBase: a floor beam under its design load, just within the limit.
# - FloorOverload: the same beam with double the load, so double the stress.
# - FloorTall: the base load on a beam 0.3 m instead of 0.2 m tall; stress
#   falls with the square of the height.
:ShelfLight a :BeamDesign ;
    :description "short wall-mounted shelf with light load" ;
    :span 0.8 ;
    :pointLoad 1.0 ;
    :width 0.04 ;
    :height 0.06 ;
    :allowableStress 12000.0 .

:FloorBase a :BeamDesign ;
    :description "base floor beam under design load" ;
    :span 3.0 ;
    :pointLoad 5.0 ;
    :width 0.05 ;
    :height 0.2 ;
    :allowableStress 12000.0 .

:FloorOverload a :BeamDesign ;
    :description "same beam as FloorBase but roughly double the load" ;
    :span 3.0 ;
    :pointLoad 10.0 ;
    :width 0.05 ;
    :height 0.2 ;
    :allowableStress 12000.0 .

:FloorTall a :BeamDesign ;
    :description "same load as FloorBase but with a taller beam" ;
    :span 3.0 ;
    :pointLoad 5.0 ;
    :width 0.05 ;
    :height 0.3 ;
    :allowableStress 12000.0 .

# Queries: print each design's bending stress, safety factor and verdict.
{
    ?Subject :bendingStress ?Value .
} log:query {
    ?Subject :bendingStress ?Value .
} .

{
    ?Subject :safetyFactor ?Value .
} log:query {
    ?Subject :safetyFactor ?Value .
} .

{
    ?Subject :isSafe ?Value .
} log:query {
    ?Subject :isSafe ?Value .
} .
